  ✕ Recursive interface embedding
   ╭─[test.lis:6:11]
 5 │ 
 6 │ interface B<T> {
   ·           ┬
   ·           ╰── creates a cycle
 7 │   embed A<Slice<T>>
   ╰────
  help: Interface embedding cycle detected: B → A → B. Break the cycle by removing one of the embeddings · code: [infer.interface_cycle]

  ✕ Cannot derive equality
    ╭─[test.lis:12:3]
 11 │ struct Wrap<T: A<T>> {
 12 │   value: T
    ·   ──┬──
    ·     ╰── `value` cannot be compared
 13 │ }
    ╰────
  help: `T` has no bound that supports comparison. Bound `T` by `Comparable`, `Ordered`, or an interface that declares `equals`, or give `Wrap` a hand-written `equals` method · code: [attribute.cannot_derive_equality]
